VeridianOS: comic applet: no out-of-range read for an identifier without ':'

Real bug (found by the patch review; present on upstream master too):
ComicEngine::requestSource() splits the identifier at ':' and read
parts[1] to decide whether the current strip is requested, before the
"Less than two arguments specified" check further down. An identifier
without ':' gives a one-element list, so parts[1] was an out-of-range
access (an assertion in debug builds, undefined behaviour otherwise).
isCurrentComic now requires the second part to exist; such an identifier
then takes the existing error path (or, offline, the cache lookup with
isCurrentComic false, as for any non-current strip). Valid identifiers
are unaffected.

--- a/applets/comic/engine/comic.cpp
+++ b/applets/comic/engine/comic.cpp
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
 
     const QStringList parts = identifier.split(QLatin1Char(':'), Qt::KeepEmptyParts);
 
-    bool isCurrentComic = parts[1].isEmpty();
+    bool isCurrentComic = parts.count() > 1 && parts[1].isEmpty();
 
     // check whether it is cached, make sure second part present
     bool lookInCache = parts.count() > 1 && !(isCurrentComic && reason == RequestReason::Check) && CachedProvider::isCached(identifier);
